 "notes": "CardDemo's card update (transaction CCUP, program COCRDUPC), a conversation over several tasks whose state travels in the COMMAREA (CCUP-CHANGE-ACTION and the details last shown): a search reads the card; an edit validates the name (alphabetic), status (Y/N), expiry month (1-12) and year (1950-2099) and asks for PF5; PF5 reads the card FOR UPDATE, refuses if it changed since it was shown, and REWRITEs it; PF3 SYNCPOINTs and returns. Each scenario's card file is compared after the task. The scenarios that start mid-conversation set that state as the program itself leaves it. Every file is the corpus's own data. Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own. A defect of the original the proof shows: the REWRITE record takes its CVV from CCUP-NEW-CVV-CD, which no input sets, so a confirmed update replaces the card's CVV (747) with blanks -- in a PIC 9(3) field, invalid numeric data whose bytes are GnuCOBOL's (IBM's MOVE may repair the sign nibble)."
}
